  "executive_briefing": "The 2026 fiscal landscape is defined by the crystallization of the OECD Pillar Two 15% global minimum tax as an operational standard, while geopolitical volatility continues to disrupt multinational supply chains through aggressive, often litigated, tariff measures. A notable shift in international tax policy is the move away from traditional corporate tax rate competition toward non-taxable fiscal incentives, such as direct investment grants, as countries seek to maintain competitiveness without triggering Pillar Two top-up taxes. Concurrently, jurisdictions are intensifying digital tax enforcement, with Singapore\u2019s mandated rollout of the InvoiceNow e-invoicing system serving as a regional blueprint for eliminating VAT/GST compliance gaps.",
